{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.ExteriorSquareBorromean","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.ExteriorSquareBorromean","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.lambda_2_C10_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.lambda_2_C10_sum","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/exterior-square-borromean.lean#L50-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.lambda_2_C10_irreducibles","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.lambda_2_C10_irreducibles","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/exterior-square-borromean.lean#L46-L48","doc":"The exterior square decomposition as a sum of irreducible\ndimensions (V_(9,1) and V_(8,1,1)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.borromean_strand_pair_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.borromean_strand_pair_count","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/exterior-square-borromean.lean#L38-L44","doc":"**Corollary.** The strand-pair count (10 choose 2) = 45 is the\ndimension of an irreducible-DIRECT-SUM in S_10's representation\ntheory, NOT a coincidence.  This is the categorical origin of\n\"45\" in the α_EM formula. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.exterior_square_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.exterior_square_decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/exterior-square-borromean.lean#L29-L36","doc":"**Decomposition theorem (S_10 representation).**\nΛ²(C^10) = V_(9,1) ⊕ V_(8,1,1) under S_10, with dimensions\n9 and 36 respectively, summing to 45. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.exterior_square_C10","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.exterior_square_C10","kind":"theorem","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/exterior-square-borromean.lean#L24-L27","doc":"**Theorem.** dim Λ²(C^10) = 45. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.exterior_square_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.exterior_square_dim","kind":"def","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/exterior-square-borromean.lean#L21-L22","doc":"Dimension of the exterior square of an n-dimensional vector space. ","signatureChunk":0}]}